   {
    "id": "note-56",
    "type": "note",
    "x": 1260,
    "y": 136,
    "text": "How to read it",
    "color": "#b8925a",
    "size": 24
   },
   {
    "id": "note-57",
    "type": "note",
    "x": 1260,
    "y": 172,
    "text": "WPA = win rate − how likely those players were to\nwin anyway (after draft). Positive means the pick\nadded win chance on average.\n\"Noise\" is my rough 95% margin from sample size\nalone. It ignores error in coachless's own model.",
    "color": "#e9dfc9",
    "size": 16
   },
   {
    "id": "note-58",
    "type": "note",
    "x": 1260,
    "y": 330,
    "text": "What it says",
    "color": "#b8925a",
    "size": 24
   },
   {
    "id": "note-59",
    "type": "note",
    "x": 1260,
    "y": 366,
    "text": "• Flash is in 99.9% of games, so its WPA of 0.00\ncan't be measured. It's a given, not a verdict.\n• The real choice is the second spell. Barrier leads\nat +0.70 over 12,192 games.\n• Barrier vs Ghost: a 1.5 pp gap, about 1.7× its\nstandard error. A lean, not proof.\n• Teleport and Exhaust have ~1.1K to 1.3K games\neach, so ±3 pp of noise. Too few to rank them.",
    "color": "#e9dfc9",
    "size": 16
   },
   {
    "id": "note-60",
    "type": "note",
    "x": 1260,
    "y": 620,
    "text": "Why Barrier might suit Kog'Maw",
    "color": "#b8925a",
    "size": 24
   },
   {
    "id": "note-61",
    "type": "note",
    "x": 1260,
    "y": 656,
    "text": "• No dash: fights are decided in short burst\nwindows.\n• At lv 18 Barrier blocks 460 and is back every\n180s. Heal restores 318 to you and an ally, every\n240s.\n• Barrier ignores Grievous Wounds and works at full\nHP.\nA hypothesis from the wiki numbers, not something\nthese stats prove.",
    "color": "#e9dfc9",
    "size": 16
   },
